1. PARTIES

   Buyer:  {{ buyer_name }}
   Seller: {{ seller_name }}

2. PROPERTY

   Address: {{ property_address }}, {{ property_city }}, {{ property_state }} {{ property_zip }}
   Legal Description: To be provided by title company at closing.
   Parcel/ATTOM ID: {{ attom_id | default('TBD') }}

3. PURCHASE PRICE

   The total purchase price is {{ purchase_price_formatted }} ({{ purchase_price_words }}).

   Earnest Money Deposit (EMD): {{ emd_formatted }} to be delivered within 3 business days
   of execution to an escrow account designated by the title company.

4. FINANCING

   This is an ALL-CASH offer. Buyer's obligation is not contingent on financing.

5. INSPECTION AND DUE DILIGENCE

   Buyer shall have {{ inspection_period_days }} calendar days from the execution date
   ("Inspection Period") to conduct any and all due diligence, including but not limited
   to physical inspection, title review, and financial analysis. During the Inspection
   Period, Buyer may terminate this Agreement for any reason by written notice to Seller,
   and the EMD shall be returned to Buyer in full. Failure to terminate in writing by
   the end of the Inspection Period constitutes Buyer's acceptance of the property.

6. CLOSING

   Closing shall occur on or before {{ closing_date }} at a title company mutually
   agreed upon by the parties. Time is of the essence.

7. ASSIGNABILITY

   BUYER MAY ASSIGN THIS AGREEMENT AND ALL OF BUYER'S RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS HEREUNDER
   TO ANY PERSON OR ENTITY WITHOUT SELLER'S CONSENT. Buyer's assignee shall assume all
   of Buyer's obligations under this Agreement upon assignment, and Buyer shall be
   released from further liability. The assignability of this contract is a material
   term relied upon by Buyer.

8. TITLE

   Seller shall convey marketable fee simple title by General Warranty Deed, free and
   clear of all liens and encumbrances except current year real estate taxes (prorated
   to closing), utility easements of record, and restrictions of record that do not
   materially impair the use of the property.

9. POSSESSION

   Seller shall deliver possession of the property at closing in its current "AS-IS"
   condition, free of all personal property not included in this sale, and broom clean.

10. AS-IS SALE

    Buyer accepts the property in its AS-IS, WHERE-IS condition. Seller makes no
    warranties, express or implied, as to the condition of the property, its fitness
    for any particular purpose, or compliance with any law or code.

11. DEFAULT

    If Seller defaults, Buyer may pursue any remedy available at law or equity.
    If Buyer defaults, Seller's sole remedy shall be retention of the EMD as
    liquidated damages.

12. ENTIRE AGREEMENT

    This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes
    all prior negotiations, representations, and agreements. This Agreement may be
    amended only by a written instrument signed by both parties.

13. GOVERNING LAW

    This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the State of Indiana.

